COMMENT     REFSEQ INFORMATION: The reference sequence is identical to
            AP005147.1.
            Plasmid R64 carries a highly mobile DNA segment designated
            'shufflon'. The DNA sequence presented below corresponds to that of
            one specific clone, pKK010-85, which was fixed because of the lack
            of rci gene encoding shufflon-specific recombinase. The results
            indicate that the shufflon is a biological switch to select one of
            seven pilV genes encoding preadhesins in which N-tertminal region
            is constant, while C-terminal region is variable.
            The annotation was added by the NCBI Prokaryotic Genome Annotation
            Pipeline (PGAP). Information about PGAP can be found here:
            https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/genome/annotation_prok/
            
